RCP 1
M title Kimchi fried rice (kimchi bokkeumbap)
M serves 2
M time 25
I 300|g|kimchi, well fermented, chopped
I 2|tbsp|kimchi juice
I 400|g|cooked short-grain rice, day-old
I 2|tbsp|vegetable oil
I 1|tbsp|gochujang
I 1|tsp|soy sauce
I 1|tsp|sesame oil
I 2||spring onions, sliced
I 2||eggs
I 1|sheet|gim (roasted seaweed), crumbled
S 0
T Heat the vegetable oil in a wide pan
T over medium-high heat.
S 240
T Fry the chopped kimchi until it softens
T and smells sweet.
S 0
T Add the gochujang and kimchi juice and
T stir through.
S 300
T Add the rice, breaking clumps, and fry,
T pressing it into the pan so it catches a
T little.
S 0
T Season with soy sauce and sesame oil;
T fold in most of the spring onion.
S 180
T Fry the eggs sunny side up in a separate
T pan.
S 0
T Serve topped with the egg, remaining
T spring onion and crumbled gim.
